ype":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PRF"},{"text":" lets a relying party derive deterministic symmetric secrets from a credential","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"— the same input produces the same output every time the user authenticates with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that credential. It’s the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/www.w3.org\/TR\/webauthn-3\/#prf-extension"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for credential-bound key derivation, built on the CTAP2 ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hmac-secret"},{"text":" extension.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The SDK transforms each PRF input with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SHA-256(\"WebAuthn PRF\\0\" || input)"},{"text":" before","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sending it to the authenticator — that domain separation is mandated by the spec.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In a high-level WebAuthn flow, configure ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PRF"},{"text":" per ceremony via","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Extension\/RegistrationInputs\/prf"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Extension\/AuthenticationInputs\/prf"},{"text":"; outputs come back on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clientExtensionResults"},{"text":" of the corresponding ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Response"},{"text":". Registration enables","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"PRF on a credential, optionally deriving